       </table><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">(1) Primarily includes other income (expense), certain one-time, non-recurring or non-cash items, and items not necessarily indicative of our underlying operating performance.</span></p><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">(2) See definition in Item 2 under Non-GAAP Financial Measures.</span></p></ix:continuation></div></ix:continuation></div><div><ix:nonNumeric id="F_e109d9c0-02a8-4676-9ebc-d5db131500b9" contextRef="C_f0bf6c77-6612-417d-8868-b7d48b232dbc" name="us-gaap:EarningsPerShareTextBlock" escape="true" continuedAt="F_e109d9c0-02a8-4676-9ebc-d5db131500b9_1"><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:18pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;" id="note_18_earnings_per_share"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">NOTE 17 &#8212; EAR</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">NINGS PER SHARE</span></p><p style="text-indent:4.533%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:8pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Basic earnings per share (&#8220;EPS&#8221;) is calculated by dividing net income (loss) available to common stockholders by the weighted average number of common shares outstanding during the period and includes vested, unissued RSUs. Diluted EPS is calculated by dividing net income (loss) available to common stockholders by the weighted average number of common shares outstanding, after giving effect to all potential dilutive common shares outstanding during the period. We include all common stock share equivalents granted under our stock-based compensation plan which remain unvested and shares used as consideration in the Ault acquisition which remain unissued (&#8220;dilutive securities&#8221;), in the number of shares outstanding for our diluted EPS calculations using the treasury method.</span></p><div style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_312a48d4-7440-470b-8e1b-b9f09daa0418" contextRef="C_f0bf6c77-6612-417d-8868-b7d48b232dbc" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfEarningsPerShareBasicAndDilutedTableTextBlock" escape="true"><p style="text-indent:4.587%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:8pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:8pt;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Basic and diluted EPS were calculated as follows:</span></p>
